  "description": "Overview Date: 14th Nov 2026 (Saturday) Registrations: Now Open Kickoff Session: 14th Nov 2026 (Saturday) [ Mandatory ] Join the WhatsApp Group for All Hackathon Updates & Details: https://chat.whatsapp.com/FWkOZgbMnqB3sKVOLnqOcD?s=cl&p=a&iam=2 This is a one-day, hands-on hackathon for individuals who want to build and launch a working AI product. What You’ll Do During the hackathon, participants will conceptualize, build, and demonstrate an agentic AI solution to a practical, real-world challenge. You’ll work through the complete product development process: Identify the problem. Design the system architecture. Integrate tools and APIs. Build and demonstrate a functional end product. The core focus is on building AI agents that can: Reason and make decisions. Interact with tools. Execute tasks independently. By the end of the day, you’ll have a working prototype that you can add to your portfolio, demonstrate in interviews, and develop further for real-world use. Participation Guidelines Join individually or in a team. Teams of up to two members are recommended. All development must take place within the hackathon timeframe on 31st October 2026. You may use AI tools, APIs, and frameworks. Clearly document your process, including the problem, solution, and architecture. A functional prototype or live demo is required. Submission Requirements Submit the following before the announced deadline on 31st October 2026: A demo video or access to a live working product. Access to the codebase through GitHub or an equivalent platform. A brief explanation of your solution. Rules Fully pre-built solutions are not allowed. Starter templates are acceptable. Copying or plagiarism will result in disqualification. Clearly distinguish your contribution from AI-generated output. Submissions must demonstrate working functionality. Designs or presentations alone will not qualify. All entries must be submitted before the deadline.",
