    "details": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 14th Nov 2026 (Saturday)</li>\n<li><strong>Registrations:</strong> Now Open</li>\n<li><strong>Kickoff Session:</strong> 14th Nov 2026 (Saturday)</li>\n<li>[ <strong>Mandatory</strong> ] Join the WhatsApp Group for All Hackathon Updates &amp; Details: <a href=\"https://chat.whatsapp.com/FWkOZgbMnqB3sKVOLnqOcD?s=cl&amp;p=a&amp;iam=2\">https://chat.whatsapp.com/FWkOZgbMnqB3sKVOLnqOcD?s=cl&amp;p=a&amp;iam=2</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>This is a one-day, hands-on hackathon for individuals who want to build and launch a working AI product.</p>\n<p><strong>What You&rsquo;ll Do</strong></p>\n<p>During the hackathon, participants will conceptualize, build, and demonstrate an agentic AI solution to a practical, real-world challenge.</p>\n<p>You&rsquo;ll work through the complete product development process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify the problem.</li>\n<li>Design the system architecture.</li>\n<li>Integrate tools and APIs.</li>\n<li>Build and demonstrate a functional end product.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The core focus is on building AI agents that can:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reason and make decisions.</li>\n<li>Interact with tools.</li>\n<li>Execute tasks independently.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>By the end of the day, you&rsquo;ll have a working prototype that you can add to your portfolio, demonstrate in interviews, and develop further for real-world use.</p>\n<p><strong>Participation Guidelines</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Join individually or in a team. Teams of up to two members are recommended.</li>\n<li>All development must take place within the hackathon timeframe on 31st October 2026.</li>\n<li>You may use AI tools, APIs, and frameworks.</li>\n<li>Clearly document your process, including the problem, solution, and architecture.</li>\n<li>A functional prototype or live demo is required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Submit the following before the announced deadline on 31st October 2026:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A demo video or access to a live working product.</li>\n<li>Access to the codebase through GitHub or an equivalent platform.</li>\n<li>A brief explanation of your solution.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully pre-built solutions are not allowed. Starter templates are acceptable.</li>\n<li>Copying or plagiarism will result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Clearly distinguish your contribution from AI-generated output.</li>\n<li>Submissions must demonstrate working functionality. Designs or presentations alone will not qualify.</li>\n<li>All entries must be submitted before the deadline.</li>\n</ul>",
